From 0f7955ec6e00fc2f472e3806c5342183532c0389 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 20:21:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(chat): stack tool strip toggle above tool list, drop
 fixed height
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

.tool-calls-panel was flex-direction:row with flex:0 0 26px, so the
'Calling N tools' toggle and the expanded tool items sat side by side in
one row and the panel height was locked to 26px — on narrow screens the
tool name got truncated to 'execute_c…' and expanded detail was
squeezed.

- panel: flex-wrap:wrap + flex:0 0 auto (height adapts to content)
- .tool-strip-body: flex:1 1 100% so the tool list wraps to its own
  full-width row below the toggle
---
 packages/client/src/components/hermes/chat/MessageList.vue | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/client/src/components/hermes/chat/MessageList.vue b/packages/client/src/components/hermes/chat/MessageList.vue
index 5c0193eb..e9e145ed 100644
--- a/packages/client/src/components/hermes/chat/MessageList.vue
+++ b/packages/client/src/components/hermes/chat/MessageList.vue
@@ -1893,9 +1893,9 @@ defineExpose({
 
 .tool-calls-panel {
   display: flex;
-  flex: 0 0 26px;
+  flex: 0 0 auto;
   flex-direction: row;
-  flex-wrap: nowrap;
+  flex-wrap: wrap;
   align-items: stretch;
   gap: 4px;
   width: 520px;
@@ -1965,6 +1965,7 @@ defineExpose({
 
 .tool-strip-body {
   display: flex;
+  flex: 1 1 100%;
   flex-direction: column;
   gap: 4px;
   width: 100%;
-- 
2.53.0

